# Consistency Report: Card-Preview CSS vs Anki Sync

**Repo:** `D:/_installed/VScode repos/AI/Cursor/Obsidian-Anki-AST-Engine`  
**Layers compared:**
- **A** — CSS visualization (`plugin/styles.css` + CM decorations)
- **B** — Preview / `cardSyntax` resolution (`src/cardSyntax/*`, `plugin/src/cardPreview*.ts`)
- **C** — Live Anki sync (`src/syncPipeline.ts` → `stateMachine` → `anki/syncEngine.ts`)

---

## 1. Executive summary

**Verdict: Layers A and B are largely consistent with each other; both diverge sharply from Layer C.**

Card preview (badge tint, cardblock outcome classes, delimiter garnishes, cloze hatch colors) is driven by `parseCardDocument` / `cardSyntax` outcomes. Spot-check of `plugin/src/cardPreviewEditor.ts` confirms decorations apply `--${displayOutcome}` and type garnishes from the same `ResolvedCard` model — so **A ↔ B holds**.

Live sync (`runSync`) does **not** import `cardSyntax`. It extracts cards via `extractCards` in `src/parser/stateMachine.ts` and always writes **Basic Front/Back** (`noteModelName` default `"Basic"` in `src/config/configParser.ts`, fields built in `src/anki/syncEngine.ts`). Cloze, reversible, typed, and custom types are resolved and visualized in preview but are **not wired into Anki write-back**.

**Top risk:** A green “Cloze” / “Typed” / “Reversible” badge (outcome ≈ sync) does **not** mean Anki receives that note type. Layout `skip`/`error` in preview also does **not** stop Layer C from writing a Basic note.

---

## 2. Architecture split

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  subgraph LayerA ["Layer A — CSS"]
    CSS["plugin/styles.css<br/>anki-card-preview-*"]
  end

  subgraph LayerB ["Layer B — Preview / cardSyntax"]
    PD["parseCardDocument"]
    TR["typeResolver + layoutValidator"]
    CP["cardPreviewEditor decorations<br/>badge / cardblock / delimiter / cloze"]
    PD --> TR --> CP
    CP --> CSS
  end

  subgraph LayerC ["Layer C — Anki sync"]
    SP["syncPipeline.runSync"]
    SM["parser/stateMachine.extractCards"]
    CC["compileCardFields → Front/Back HTML"]
    SE["anki/syncEngine<br/>addNote/updateNoteFields<br/>modelName = noteModelName (Basic)"]
    SP --> SM --> CC --> SE
  end

  MD["Markdown note<br/>AnkiSync + H4 + :::"] --> PD
  MD --> SP

  CP -.->|"NO import"| SP
  PD -.->|"cardSyntax NOT used by sync"| SP
```

| Concern | Layer A | Layer B | Layer C |
|--------|---------|---------|---------|
| Entry | `styles.css` classes | `plugin/src/cardPreview.ts` → `parseCardDocument` | `plugin/src/syncOrchestrator.ts` → `runSync` |
| Parser | — | `src/cardSyntax/*` | `src/parser/stateMachine.ts` |
| Types | Badge text + delimiter garnish + cloze marks (no per-type block tints) | `basic` / `cloze` / `reversible` / `typed` / `custom` | Always Basic Front/Back |
| Gate | Decorations only if `syncEligible` | `shouldSync(frontmatter)` (`ankisync: true`) | `shouldSyncFile` (same gate) |
| Outcome vocabulary | `--sync` / `--warn` / `--skip` / `--error` | Same via `SyncOutcome` | add / update / skip / fail (different semantics: duplicates, unchanged fields, etc.) |

**Design doc:** `Docs/DECIDING/Card-Preview-Design-Guidelines.md` describes Layer A/B intent; it does not claim Layer C implements multi-type write-back.

---

## 3. Consistent areas

| Concept | A | B | C | Notes |
|---------|---|---|---|-------|
| Frontmatter sync gate | Decorations suppressed when ineligible | `parseCardDocument` → `syncEligible: false` if `ankisync` not true | `shouldSyncFile` skips file | Shared `src/io/frontmatterFilter.ts` |
| Card declaration heading level | Covered lines under `####` (default) | `cardDeclarationHeadingLevel` (default 4) | Same option passed into `extractCards` | Both read frontmatter / settings |
| Structural `:::` split existence | Delimiter guide on primary ::: line | Layout expects plain `:::` for basic | `findDelimiterIndex` splits on configured delimiter (default `:::`) | Shared *concept*; typed variants differ (below) |
| HTML Front/Back envelopes for basic cards | Block tint around heading→body | Resolves text/back regions | Compiles `frontNodes`/`backNodes` to HTML | For plain basic F/B, intent aligns |
| `<!--anki-id: uuid-->` awareness | Not CSS-visible | Parsed for card identity in cardSyntax | Extracted in stateMachine; drives update vs add | B+C both know IDs; A does not show them |
| Tags & decks (conceptual presence) | Not CSS | Hashtags / file defaults partially modeled | `file_anki_tags`, `target_anki_deck`, heading tag, UUID tags written | Data exists on sync; preview does not decorate it |
| Outcome vocabulary (names) | `--sync/warn/skip/error` | Same enum + messages | Different action enum, but “skip” exists | Names overlap; **meaning** of skip diverges |
| Mid-HR / tables / section-start / inter-card gap | CSS + layout helpers | Covered-line painting in editor | Sync ignores presentation | Consistent that these are **preview-only chrome** |

**A ↔ B alignment (spot-check):** In `buildCardPreviewDecorations`, each covered line gets `anki-card-preview-cardblock--${badgeModel.displayOutcome}`; badges use the same `displayOutcome` from `effectivePreviewOutcome(card)`. Cloze marks require `resolvedType.type === 'cloze'`. Delimiter garnish classes (`--info` / `--typed` / `--reversible`) come from `buildDelimiterLineDecorations` → `buildDelimiterGuideClasses`. **Layer A faithfully paints Layer B.**

---

## 4. Inconsistent / divergent areas

| User-visible claim | Layer A+B | Layer C | Impact |
|--------------------|-----------|---------|--------|
| Badge “Cloze” (often with sync tint) | Type resolved; cloze tokens colored; may outcome=`sync` | Writes Basic note; `{{cN::…}}` compiled as ordinary HTML in Front/Back | User believes cloze note type will exist in Anki |
| Badge “Reversible” + ↑↓ garnish on `:::` / `:::r` | Builtin reversible | Basic Front/Back only — no reverse card generation | Reverse cards never created |
| Badge “Typed” + ⌨ garnish on `:::` / `:::t` | Builtin typed + typed-layout warnings | Basic Front/Back; typed answer not special-cased | No type-in answer model |
| Badge “Custom … note type” | Resolves `#anki/noteType/…` / field blocks | Still `modelName: config.noteModelName` (Basic) with only Front/Back | Custom models never selected |
| Outcome `skip` / `error` (layout rules BAS-01, CLZ-01, CLZ-11, etc.) | Tint + badge suffix ⛔/❌; implies will not sync | `layoutValidator` **not** consulted; card still queued for add/update | False confidence that bad layouts are blocked |
| `:::r` / `:::t` lines | First-class delimiter kinds in cardSyntax | `delimiterCheck` matches `:::` via `indexOf(":::")`, so `:::r` splits after `:::`; suffix `r`/`t` can leak into Back | Preview treats as typed delimiter; sync may leave letter remnant |
| Manual `{{}}` on basic + `inferClozeFromManualSyntaxOnBasic` | Preview reclassifies as cloze (settings toggle in `plugin/src/settings.ts`) | Sync never switches model; literals remain in Basic fields | Setting name promises sync behavior; only affects preview |
| Preview outcome `warn` | Yellow tint; still “will sync” semantics for B | Sync may succeed without surfacing those warnings | Warnings are authoring-only |
| Reading mode | Partial `.markdown-preview-view` badge CSS in `styles.css` | N/A | Styles exist but **no** `registerMarkdownPostProcessor` — Reading Mode unwired (`cardPreview.ts` only registers editor extension) |

